<title>CANADA: Canadian foreign reserves rise in June.</title>
<headline>Canadian foreign reserves rise in June.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian foreign reserve holdings rose in June, the Finance Department said on Friday.</p>
<p>   RESERVES			  June 97	May 97</p>
<p>   Total			   21.258 bln  21.025 bln</p>
<p>   U.S. dollars		  18.338 bln  18.084 bln</p>
<p>   Other foreign currencies     502 million     515 million</p>
<p>   Gold				 150 million     150 million</p>
<p>   Special drawing rights     1.142 bln   1.146 bln</p>
<p>   IMF reserves		   1.126 bln   1.130 bln</p>
<p>Note - Figures in U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Official government operations decreased reserves by US$283 million.</p>
<p>Details of the changes in the month:</p>
<p>    Gain on gold sales		   n/a</p>
<p>    Earnings on investments	    +90</p>
<p>    Revaluation effects		  -10</p>
<p>    Foreign currency debt	     +445</p>
<p>    Other transactions		    -9</p>
<p>NOTE - in millions of U.S. dollars  </p>
<p>During June, net sales of Canada bills increased by $455.1 million to a level of outstanding bills of $5.893 billion. Sales of Canada notes decreased by $10 million to a level of outstanding notes of $1.292 billion.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
